@@ -293,6 +294,13 @@ state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transi
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
 again.
 
+Command mode supports Vim-style visual selection on the focused pane. `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V` start
+character, line, and block selections; movement keys and arrows extend the internal selection; `y`
+copies the selected text; and `Y` copies whole selected lines. Copy output is emitted as an OSC 52
+clipboard sequence in the next rendered frame. Selection rendering is owned by `TerminalUi`, while
+`TerminalApp` and `UiHarness` pass the current right-pane content and chat cursor column into the UI
+state machine so selections and copies are based on the focused rendered text.
+
 `src/ui.rs::TerminalUi` owns terminal-specific presentation state:
 
 - `UiMode`, `PaneFocus`, `UiSurface`, `UiKey`, and `UiAction` model terminal interactions.
